{"$schema":"https://json.schemastore.org/sarif-2.1.0.json","runs":[{"artifacts":[{"contents":{"text":"<scxml xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml\" version=\"1.0\" datamodel=\"xpath\" initial=\"a\">\n  <datamodel><data id=\"list\"><item xmlns=\"\">1</item><item xmlns=\"\">2</item></data></datamodel>\n  <state id=\"a\">\n    <onentry>\n      <assign location=\"$list/item[0]\" expr=\"5\"/>\n    </onentry>\n    <transition event=\"go\" cond=\"$list/item[0] = 1\" target=\"b\"/>\n  </state>\n  <final id=\"b\"/>\n</scxml>\n"},"location":{"uri":"tests/ui/lint013-xpath-zero-position.scx"},"mimeType":"application/scxml+xml"}],"columnKind":"utf16CodeUnits","properties":{"diagnosticCounts":{"errors":0,"notes":0,"total":2,"warnings":2},"producer":{"kind":"validator"}},"results":[{"fixes":[{"artifactChanges":[{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/lint013-xpath-zero-position.scx"},"replacements":[{"deletedRegion":{"byteLength":1,"byteOffset":253,"endColumn":37,"endLine":5,"startColumn":36,"startLine":5},"insertedContent":{"text":"1"}}]}],"description":{"text":"select the first node with `[1]`"},"properties":{"applicability":"maybe-incorrect"}}],"level":"warning","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/lint013-xpath-zero-position.scx"},"region":{"endColumn":38,"endLine":5,"startColumn":35,"startLine":5}}}],"message":{"markdown":"the predicate `[0]` selects no node: XPath positions start at 1\n\n**Note:** a numeric predicate `[n]` keeps only the node at position `n`, and XPath counts positions from 1, so no node is at position 0; assigning to a location that selects no node raises `error.execution`\n\n**Help:** XPath positions start at 1: select the first node with `[1]` (and the last with `[last()]`)\n\n**Spec:** SCXML CR 2014 §C.3 The XPath Data Model\n\n**Spec:** XPath 1.0 §2.4 Predicates","text":"the predicate `[0]` selects no node: XPath positions start at 1"},"properties":{"byteSpan":{"end":255,"start":252},"category":"lint"},"relatedLocations":[{"id":1,"message":{"text":"in this `location`"},"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/lint013-xpath-zero-position.scx"},"region":{"endColumn":38,"endLine":5,"startColumn":25,"startLine":5}}}],"ruleId":"LINT013"},{"fixes":[{"artifactChanges":[{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/lint013-xpath-zero-position.scx"},"replacements":[{"deletedRegion":{"byteLength":1,"byteOffset":327,"endColumn":46,"endLine":7,"startColumn":45,"startLine":7},"insertedContent":{"text":"1"}}]}],"description":{"text":"select the first node with `[1]`"},"properties":{"applicability":"maybe-incorrect"}}],"level":"warning","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/lint013-xpath-zero-position.scx"},"region":{"endColumn":47,"endLine":7,"startColumn":44,"startLine":7}}}],"message":{"markdown":"the predicate `[0]` selects no node: XPath positions start at 1\n\n**Note:** a numeric predicate `[n]` keeps only the node at position `n`, and XPath counts positions from 1, so no node is at position 0; an empty node-set is false, so this condition never holds\n\n**Help:** XPath positions start at 1: select the first node with `[1]` (and the last with `[last()]`)\n\n**Spec:** SCXML CR 2014 §C.3 The XPath Data Model\n\n**Spec:** XPath 1.0 §2.4 Predicates","text":"the predicate `[0]` selects no node: XPath positions start at 1"},"properties":{"byteSpan":{"end":329,"start":326},"category":"lint"},"relatedLocations":[{"id":1,"message":{"text":"in this `cond`"},"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/lint013-xpath-zero-position.scx"},"region":{"endColumn":51,"endLine":7,"startColumn":34,"startLine":7}}}],"ruleId":"LINT013"}],"tool":{"driver":{"informationUri":"https://www.w3.org/TR/scxml/","name":"scxml-validator","rules":[{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"a numeric predicate `[n]` keeps only the node at position `n`, and XPath counts positions from 1, so `[0]` (the ECMAScript habit of indexing from 0), a negative number, or a fraction selects nothing: a location that selects nothing raises `error.execution`, a condition is false, and a value is empty"},"help":{"text":"How to fix: select the first node with `[1]` and the last with `[last()]`.\n\nSpecification: XPath 1.0 §2.4 Predicates\n\nRun `scx --explain LINT013` for examples."},"helpUri":"https://www.w3.org/TR/1999/REC-xpath-19991116/#predicates","id":"LINT013","name":"LINT013","properties":{"category":"lint"},"shortDescription":{"text":"an XPath predicate selects by a position that no node has"}}],"semanticVersion":"0.2.0"}}}],"version":"2.1.0"}